---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { routeUrl } from '../../i18n';

const lang = 'en' as const;
const lastUpdated = 'June 22, 2026';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of service · Accanto"
  description="Terms governing the use of the Accanto app: service scope, account, user content, liability, withdrawal."
>
  <article class="container-page container-prose">
    <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Terms</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold mb-4">Terms of service</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-accanto-500 mb-6">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <aside class="rounded-lg border border-accanto-200 bg-accanto-50 p-4 mb-8 text-sm">
      The authoritative version of these terms is published in Italian at
      <a href="/it/termini" class="underline font-semibold">/it/termini</a>. The English summary
      below mirrors its key points; in case of conflict the Italian text prevails.
    </aside>

    <h2>Service provider</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>PRESTIA.DEV S.A.S. DI PRESTIA ANDREA</strong> — Viale Bruno Rizzieri 199C, 00173 Rome
      (RM), Italy. VAT IT17486541000. REA RM-1721153.<br />
      Contact: <a href="mailto:support@accanto.care">support@accanto.care</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Scope</h2>
    <p>Accanto is a digital tool to organize information, notes, documents and tasks related to
    caring for a family member. It is shared within "care circles" with the members you invite. It
    is not a medical device and does not provide diagnosis or clinical advice.</p>

    <h2>Account</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You must provide a valid email and password to use the service.</li>
      <li>You are responsible for keeping your credentials safe; we recommend enabling TOTP 2FA.</li>
      <li>You must be at least 16 years old (younger users need a parent/guardian's consent).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>User content</h2>
    <p>Everything you enter in Accanto remains yours. You grant us a limited license to store,
    process and display it strictly to operate the service. You are responsible for the content
    you provide and, in particular, for being entitled to process third-party data (e.g. the
    person you assist) under applicable law.</p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You agree not to attempt to compromise the service's security, scrape it in bulk, impersonate
    other users, or use it for unlawful activities.</p>

    <h2>Pricing</h2>
    <p>Accanto is currently free during the launch phase. Any future paid tier will be communicated
    in advance and governed by dedicated commercial terms.</p>

    <h2>Termination</h2>
    <p>You can delete your account at any time from the Account section of the app. Your data is
    erased from active systems within 30 days and from cyclic backups within an additional 60
    days, as described in the <a href={routeUrl('privacy', lang)}>Privacy notice</a>.</p>

    <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>The service is provided "as-is" and "as-available". To the extent permitted by law we
    disclaim warranties of uninterrupted or error-free operation. Mandatory consumer rights remain
    unaffected.</p>

    <h2>Medical disclaimer</h2>
    <p>Accanto is <strong>not a medical device</strong> within the meaning of Regulation (EU)
    2017/745 and does not replace professional medical advice. In case of emergency call 112 (EU)
    or your local emergency number.</p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>These terms are governed by Italian law. Any dispute that cannot be resolved amicably is
    subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of Rome, Italy, subject to mandatory
    consumer protection rules.</p>

    <p class="text-sm text-accanto-500 mt-10">
      Questions? Email <a href="mailto:support@accanto.care">support@accanto.care</a> or visit the
      <a href={routeUrl('contact', lang)}>contact</a> page.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
